What is a Volume in Kubernetes?

A Volume is storage attached to a Pod that lets containers:

persist data beyond container restarts
share files between containers in the same Pod

👉 Containers are ephemeral, but volumes give durable or shared storage.


Types of Volumes (Important)

1. emptyDir (Ephemeral)
   --------------------

Use:
Temp storage
Sharing data between containers (sidecar pattern)

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: emptydir-demo
spec:
  containers:
  - name: app
    image: nginx
    volumeMounts:
    - mountPath: /data
      name: shared-data

  - name: sidecar
    image: busybox
    command: ["sh","-c","while true; do echo hello > file.txt; sleep 5; done"]
    volumeMounts:
    - mountPath: /data
      name: shared-data

  volumes:
  - name: shared-data
    emptyDir: {}

Lifecycle: This will be Deleted when Pod is deleted


2. hostPath
   --------

	Use:
	Access node’s filesystem (for logs, system-level apps)

		volumes:
		- name: host-volume
		  hostPath:
		    path: /var/log

		⚠️ Not recommended for production (node dependency)


Persistent Volumes (PV + PVC)
Use:
	Database storage
	Long-term storage


	Admin creates PV
	User creates PVC
	Pod uses PVC → gets storage


	Example: 

	Persistent Volume (PV)

	apiVersion: v1
	kind: PersistentVolume
	metadata:
	  name: pv-demo
	spec:
	  capacity:
	    storage: 1Gi
	  accessModes:
	  - ReadWriteOnce
	  hostPath:
	    path: /mnt/data

	Persistent Volume Claim (PVC)

	apiVersion: v1
	kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
	metadata:
	  name: pvc-demo
	spec:
	  accessModes:
	  - ReadWriteOnce
	  resources:
	    requests:
	      storage: 1Gi


Pod using PVC

containers:
- name: app
  image: nginx
  volumeMounts:
  - mountPath: /usr/share/nginx/html
    name: storage

volumes:
- name: storage
  persistentVolumeClaim:
    claimName: pvc-demo


4. StorageClass (Dynamic Provisioning)

Use:
	Auto-create storage (AWS EBS, Azure Disk, etc.)
	apiVersion: storage.k8s.io/v1
	kind: StorageClass
	metadata:
	  name: fast
	provisioner: kubernetes.io/aws-ebs

	👉 No need to manually create PV